# Local secrets for `wrangler dev`. Copy to `.dev.vars` (gitignored).
#
# This worker deliberately holds no IMAP credential — the sync worker owns it,
# and writes reach that worker over a service binding (#12).
#
# Neither value below is a secret: a team domain is public and an AUD tag is an
# identifier, not a credential. In production both are `vars` in wrangler.jsonc,
# added at deploy time because this repository is public. They are repeated here
# only so `wrangler dev` can be pointed at a real tenant.

# ACCESS_TEAM_DOMAIN=https://<team>.cloudflareaccess.com
# ACCESS_AUD=<application audience tag>

# Worth knowing before you reach for `wrangler dev` at all:
#
# Cloudflare Access is not in front of a local worker, so nothing attaches a
# Cf-Access-Jwt-Assertion header to your request. With the two variables set,
# every local request is therefore answered 401; with them unset, 500. Neither
# is a bug — it is the gate failing closed, which is the whole point of it.
#
# So local work on the MCP tools happens through `pnpm run test` and
# `pnpm run test:watch`, which mint real assertions against a throwaway tenant
# (see test/support/access.ts). To drive a *deployed* instance by hand instead,
# `cloudflared access token -app=https://<your-host>` prints a real assertion
# you can pass as that header.
